{"alignments":[],"candidates":[{"additionalConceptCount":0,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 120 square meters","reason":"Each side is 52/4=13. Half of AC is 12, so half of the other diagonal is sqrt(13^2-12^2)=5. The area is 24*10/2=120.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2019_AMC_8_Q04","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"primary","label":"Use perpendicular rhombus diagonals and a 5-12-13 right triangle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"primary":["cnm_189"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_189"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: R²=3/2","reason":"For cube edge s, each section side has length √(s²+(s/2)²), so the section is a rhombus. Its diagonals are EC=s√3 and JI=s√2. Its area is s²√6/2, so R=√6/2 and R²=3/2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2018_AMC_8_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"primary","label":"Justify rhombus shape and calculate its two diagonals","methodDirectNodeIds":{"primary":["cnm_189","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_189","cnm_174"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D. The diagonals are perpendicular to each other","reason":"Parallel opposite sides, equal opposite angles, and bisecting diagonals hold for every parallelogram. Perpendicular diagonals are guaranteed for a rhombus but not for a general parallelogram.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_189_q2","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_183"],"id":"main","label":"Compare rhombus and parallelogram properties","methodDirectNodeIds":{"main":["cnm_189"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_189","cnm_183"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"20","reason":"AB = AD and angle BAD = 60°, so triangle ABD is equila